# .easignore — what EAS Build must NOT upload.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# The last build uploaded a 247 MB archive and took 7m 11s just to upload, then
# spent so long computing the project fingerprint that the local CLI hit its
# timeout and THE BUILD WAS NEVER CREATED. That is the concrete cost of this file
# not existing.
#
# The cause was measurable: the entire git repository is 260 files totalling
# 6.1 MB (biggest single file: a 1 MB icon). The other ~240 MB was `.repro*`
# scratch directories left over from debugging — gitignored, so they never
# reached the repository, but still walked and uploaded by the archiver.
# Gitignored does not reliably mean "excluded from the build".
#
# WHEN THIS FILE EXISTS, EAS USES IT INSTEAD OF .gitignore — so everything the
# build genuinely needs must be absent from here, not just everything unwanted.
# `scripts/`, `assets/`, `src/`, `App.tsx`, `index.ts`, `app.json` and
# `package-lock.json` are deliberately NOT listed below.

# --- scratch reproduction dirs (the bulk of the 247 MB) ---
.repro/
.repro2/
.repro3/
.repro4/
.repro5/
.repro6/
.repro7/
.repro8/
.repro*/

# --- dependencies: EAS installs these from package-lock.json ---
node_modules/
admin/node_modules/

# --- the admin console is a separate app and is not part of the mobile build ---
admin/

# --- the service-role key must never enter a build archive ---
# scripts/ is uploaded on purpose (tooling the build may need), which means this
# file inside it was being uploaded too. EAS keeps archives and they are
# downloadable, so the key that bypasses every RLS policy was sitting in one.
# Metro never loads it, so excluding it cannot break the bundle - that is a
# different file, .env, which stays uploaded for the reasons recorded below.
scripts/.secrets.env

# --- build / tooling caches ---
node-compile-cache/
.expo/
.expo-shared/

# --- dated brand-asset backups ---
assets/_brand-backup*/

# --- local junk ---
temp/
*.log
npm-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ============================================================
# DO NOT ADD .env, .env.local OR ANY .env.* FILE TO THIS FILE.
# Doing exactly that shipped a build that died on launch.
#
# The reasoning that produced the mistake, so it is not repeated: a comment here
# used to claim "EXPO_PUBLIC_* come from the EAS environment". That is FALSE.
# Verified with `eas env:list --environment preview` and `--environment
# production`, both of which answer "No variables found for this environment."
#
# So the ONLY source of EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL / _ANON_KEY / _GIPHY_API_KEY in
# this project is the local .env file, and Metro reads it from the uploaded
# project at build time. Exclude it and src/supabase/client.ts throws at module
# load ("Missing Supabase env vars"), which in a release build is not a red box
# but a process death: the splash appears, then the app drops back to the home
# screen. No message, nothing to search, no way for the user to tell why.
#
# Uploading it is not a secret leak. Every EXPO_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the
# JS bundle and already ships inside the APK, so these were never secret - the
# Supabase anon key is designed to be public and is enforced by RLS, not by
# being hidden.
#
# Note also that EAS was previously uploading these files ANYWAY despite them
# being listed in .gitignore - the same behaviour that pushed 239 MB of .repro*
# scratch into the archive. Gitignored did not mean excluded. This file is the
# exclusion mechanism that actually works, so what it omits matters.
# ============================================================
